<title>USA: CME July pork bellies touch three-cent limit down.</title>
<headline>CME July pork bellies touch three-cent limit down.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME July pork belly futures touched down the three-cent-per-lb limit on fund long liquidation, floor sources said.</p>
<p>ADM Investor Services, FIMAT and Refco were featured sellers, traders noted.</p>
<p>Some commercial buying was, however, noted around the day's lows. July sank to 75.900 cents but had rallied slightly by 1111 CDT to 76.300 cents, down 2.600 cents.</p>
